@startuml
title Lazy best-first extraction: enumerate ALL derivations (the no-miss heart)

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #374151
  LifeLineBorderColor #6B7280
  ParticipantBorderColor #1F2937
  ParticipantFontColor #111827
}

actor "Caller\n(report builder)" as caller #DBEAFE
participant "Extractor\n`derivations(q)`" as ex #FBCFE8
participant "ClassState[root q]" as root #FEF3C7
participant "root.cand\nper-class min-heap" as heap #DCFCE7
participant "ClassState[child c]" as child #FDE68A

caller -> ex : derivations(q).collect_checked()\n— pull ALL, best-first ordered
activate ex
ex -> root : next derivation (resumable stream)
activate root

loop until Done(completeness)  — EXHAUSTION, not a top-N cap
  root -> heap : pop best candidate\n(weight, ordered exact key)
  activate heap
  heap --> root : candidate e-node n + child ranks
  deactivate heap

  group materialize: pull each child's rankₖ-th best (internal lazy product)
    root -> child : rankₖ-th derivation of child c
    activate child
    child --> root : child derivation  (or 0̄ = refuted)
    deactivate child
  end

  alt cycle back-edge
    root -> root : mark cycle cut\n(stream ends BoundedByCycleCut)
  else exact key already emitted
    root -> root : skip duplicate\n(exact-key dedup)
  else weight = 0̄
    root -> root : refuted; keep successors
  else valid + distinct
    root -> heap : push successors\n(bump ONE child rank)
    activate heap
    deactivate heap
    root --> ex : yield this derivation\n(next stream item)
  end
end

ex --> caller : Extraction<Vec<Derivation>>\n+ Complete | BoundedByCycleCut
deactivate root
deactivate ex

note over root, child #EDE9FE
  No-miss + no-prune: the stream is COMPLETE. Pulled to
  exhaustion it yields EVERY derivation of q — weight ORDERS
  the stream, it never PRUNES. The only exclusions are
  0̄-weight (refuted) and back-edges (reported, not silently
  dropped). `kth(q, k)` is the indexed-access sibling of this
  same iterator — not a separate, truncating top-N path.
end note
@enduml
